  "narrative": [
    {
      "text": "Resurgence Analysis of Quantum Invariants of Seifert Fibered Homology Spheres — For a Seifert ﬁbered homology sphere X we show that the q-series invariant ˆZ0(X; q) introduced by\n\n**Resurgence Analysis of Quantum Invariants of Seifert Fibered Homology Spheres**\n\n*Fibered Homology Spheres*\n\n40 pp, 16 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** For a Seifert ﬁbered homology sphere X we show that the q-series invariant ˆZ0(X; q) introduced by Gukov-Pei-Putrov-Vafa, is a resummation of the Ohtsuki series Z0(X). We show that for every even k ∈N there exists a full asymptotic expansion of ˆZ0(X; q) for q tending to e2πi/k, and in particular that the limit ˆZ0(X; e2πi/k) exists and is equal to the WRT quantum invariant τk(X). We show that the poles of the Borel transform of Z0(X) coincide with the classical complex Chern-Simons values, which we further show classiﬁes the corresponding components of the moduli space of ﬂat SL(2, C)-connections.\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Complex Chern-Simons theory on X; 1.1 The moduli space and complex Chern-Simons ; 2 The Borel transform and Complex Cherns-Simon; 2.1 Resummation of the WRT invariant; 2.2 Resurgence of the generating function; 3 A resurgence formula for the GPPV invariant; 3.1 Proof of Theorem 3; 4 The asymptotic expansion of the GPPV invaria; 4.1 Proof of Theorem 4; 4.1.1 The decomposition of the GPPV invariant; 4.1.2 Asymptotic expansions of q-series with p; 4.1.3 The asymptotic expansion of the GPPV inv; Appendix A Resurgence and resummation; A.1 Resurgent functions and the Borel transfor; A.2 Borel-Laplace resummation",
